{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 409 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1bae821ec5d0b40b5a6732cbeb74b28708c11793ec50eea9df40eb2f81d80fbb" :edb/db-before-t 408 :edb/db-after-t 409 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533721 50 #inst "2026-10-04T19:09:29.911Z" 13194139533721 true] [17592186103763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248383 13194139533721 true] [17592186105624 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248377 13194139533721 true] [17592186105624 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248380 13194139533721 true] [17592186105778 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248384 13194139533721 true] [17592186105778 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248391 13194139533721 true] [17592186106209 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533721 true] [17592186106209 1145 "Applying the power rule and the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3} & =({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3})\\cdot ({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)^{3}) \\\\  & =({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3})\\cdot {({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x))}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=3.$ Therefore, the above becomes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot {(3)}^{3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =27\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph $y={x}^{3}$ is power function with an odd positive power and therefore has the property that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $27$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3}=-\\infty .\n$$" 13194139533721 true] [17592186248377 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248378 13194139533721 true] [17592186248377 1089 "q-300764" 13194139533721 true] [17592186248377 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533721 true] [175921862483